avideo-cve-2026-33500 — PatchClosure-Bench repro (REAL AVideo, real-app-http, xss-exfil canary)
================================================================================================
Pair: CVE-2026-27568 (orig, stored XSS via Parsedown, GHSA-rcqw-6466-3mv7, fixed v21.0)
   -> CVE-2026-33500 (incomplete-fix bypass, GHSA-72h5-39r7-r26j, <=26.0)
Sink : comment markdown rendering -> markDownToHTML() -> <a href> (objects/functionsSecurity.php).
Guard: ParsedownSafeWithLinks inlineMarkup()/sanitizeATag() scheme whitelist /^(https?://|mailto:|/|#)/i
       on RAW HTML <a>; safeMode OFF (V1 = commit f154167251).
Gap  : markdown link [x](url) is parsed by Parsedown CORE inlineLink() (NOT overridden in V1) ->
       javascript: href survives. Fixed V2 = commit 3ae02fa2409 (inlineLink() override, same whitelist).

RUN MODE = real-app-http (NO source-lift). Each v0/v1/v2 image `git clone`s the REAL
github.com/WWBN/AVideo tree at the exact CVE commit at build time and serves it. The sink
markDownToHTML() + ParsedownSafeWithLinks execute out of the CLONED objects/functionsSecurity.php
over the REAL vendored Parsedown (vendor/erusev/parsedown). avideo_sink.php is thin glue that
`require`s /app/vendor/autoload.php (REAL Parsedown) + /app/objects/functionsSecurity.php (REAL
sink) and calls the REAL markDownToHTML() exactly as objects/comment.php does. Nothing in this case
re-implements the sink.

Pinned commits (verified over HTTP via GET /health, which echoes AE_REF):
  v0 = 3905f03df0f0d05c44715419d7535e4dc3649e76  (pre-27568; plain Parsedown 1.7.4, safeMode default OFF)
  v1 = f154167251c9cf183ce09cd018d07e9352310457  (27568 fix = TARGET; ParsedownSafeWithLinks, NO inlineLink override) [Parsedown 1.8.0]
  v2 = 3ae02fa240939dbefc5949d64f05790fd25d728d  (33500 fix; + inlineLink() override) [Parsedown 1.8.0]
Lineage verified: `git rev-parse 3ae02fa2409^` == f154167251 (V2's parent IS V1); the V1->V2 diff on
objects/functionsSecurity.php is exactly the addition of ParsedownSafeWithLinks::inlineLink().

External HTTP entry points (all real AVideo files executing):
  POST http://127.0.0.1:3352{0,1,2}/comment   c=<attacker markdown/HTML>   (stores the comment)
  GET  http://127.0.0.1:3352{0,1,2}/           (renders it via the REAL markDownToHTML sink; page the victim views)

